  "final_message": "Calling `service.checkout(\"7781\")` writes the key `AUD-ORDER-7781` into the audit log dict. I confirmed this by running the code, not just by reading it.\n\n1. `service.checkout(\"7781\")` calls `write_audit(\"order\", \"7781\")` in `service.py`.\n2. In `audit.py`, `write_audit` sets `key = [REDACTED:SECRET]\n3. `_format_key` returns `f\"{AUDIT_PREFIX}-{kind.upper()}-{ident}\"`, and `config.py` sets `AUDIT_PREFIX = \"AUD\"`. That gives `AUD` + `ORDER` + `7781`.\n4. Running `write_audit('order', '7781')` directly printed the key `['AUD-ORDER-7781']`.\n\n`decoy_metrics.py` builds keys in the same way but with the `MET` prefix, and it never writes to the audit log. Nothing on the checkout path uses `decoy_cache.py`.\n\nANSWER: AUD-ORDER-7781",
